{title: You, You Are God}
{song_number: 162}
{language: en}
{tempo: 130}
{comment: Walker Beach}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Here I am, I've come to find You;
[F]here I am, to [C]see Your grace.
[Am]To bring to You an [G]offering,
[F]I have to ask myself [G]one thing:
[Am]How can I do anything but [Bb]praise,
[F]I [G]praise?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Here I am, I've come to thank You;
[F]here I am, a [C]life You've changed.
[Am]Because You gave Your life for [G]me,
[F]You crucified Your Son for [G]me.
[Am]How can I do anything but [Bb]praise,
[F]I [G]praise?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]You, You are God; [Bb]You are Lord;
[Am]You are all I'm [F]living for;
[C]You are King of [Bb]everything;
[Am]I want my life to [F]praise [C]You.
{end_of_chorus}
